$[Import* std]
A function head in place of a name defines a function, which may call itself.
$[# {fact n} {!if {= n 0} 1 {* n {fact {- n 1}}}}]
${fact 5}
expect: 120
Its body may start with declarations; a zero-parameter head defines a thunk.
$[# {hyp a b} [# aa {* a a} bb {* b b}] {sqrt {+ aa bb}}]
$[# {answer} 42]
${hyp 3.0 4.0} ${answer}
expect: 5.0
expect: 42
One declaration holds several bindings, in order; each sees the ones before it.
$[# base 10  {addBase x} {+ x base}  twelve {addBase 2}]
$twelve
expect: 12
Defined functions generalize like any binding.
$[# {same x} x]
${pair {same 1} {same "a"}}
expect: {first: 1, second: "a"}
Local definitions work in lambda bodies too.
${{^ {n} [# {go i acc} {!if {= i 0} acc {go {- i 1} {+ acc i}}}] {go n 0}} 100}
expect: 5050
In a definition the name is the function itself; a plain binding's expression sees the outer name instead.
$[# {scale x} {* x 10}]
${{^ {y} [# scale {^ {x} {+ {scale x} 1}}] {scale y}} 1}
expect: 11
